{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a06de069fb7942b1cc715e92a26b21","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"powder list --mine \"$POWDER_AGENT\" --repo misty-step/canopy; echo \"EXIT:$?\"\necho \"===TAKEABLE===\"\npowder list --takeable --repo misty-step/canopy; echo \"EXIT:$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-docs-discovery-alignment\",\n    \"title\": \"Document zero-config discovery mechanics and precedence in README\",\n    \"spec\": \"Align README.md with the current implementation: document systemd unit discovery (forest@*.service), checkout-local discovery conventions, configuration precedence (CLI flag \\u003e canopy.json \\u003e zero-config discovery), and empty-state requirements.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T22:09:57.811Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:09:57.811Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.217Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.217Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Align README.md with the current implementation: document systemd unit discovery (forest@*.service), checkout-local discovery conventions, configuration precedence (CLI flag \\u003e canopy.json \\u003e zero-config discovery), and empty-state requirements.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.217Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:09:57.811Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-log-drawer-experience\",\n    \"title\": \"Replace inline table log expansion with an accessible slide-over drawer\",\n    \"spec\": \"Redesign the Run log viewer to open into an accessible slide-over drawer or modal panel with fixed gutter, clean typography, and a copy button instead of expanding inline within table rows.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T22:43:58.818Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:43:58.818Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"Redesign the Run log viewer to open into an accessible slide-over drawer or modal panel with fixed gutter, clean typography, and a copy button instead of expanding inline within table rows.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-03T22:01:07.744Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:43:58.818Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\",\n    \"title\": \"Malformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:08:57.104Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:31.392Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: main.go:37-41 — when -config is absent, a malformed canopy.json (decode or validation error from LoadInventory) is silently discarded and Canopy starts with zero instances and defaults; no error is logged or surfaced. This contradicts the stated rejection policy at inventory.go:16-17 (\\\"Unknown fields are rejected so a misspelled operational setting cannot silently select a default\\\") and the loud log.Fatalf behavior of the -config path at main.go:31-33.\\nRequired: a default canopy.json that fails to load must fail loudly (or be surfaced to the operator), matching the -config path behavior.\\nProposed spec direction: treat an existing but unparseable default canopy.json as a fatal startup error, identical to -config; keep the true zero-config (no file) path unchanged.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:54:31.226Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-critic-log-sanitize-untested\",\n    \"title\": \"Log redaction (sanitizeLogText) has no regression tests\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy renders retained Run logs after `sanitizeLogText`, but no test defends this server-side credential boundary. The open log drawer adds a copy surface over the same fragment.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- Preserve benign and empty log text unchanged.\\n- Redact every currently supported credential form: `keys/`, `key_id=`/`key-id:`, `token=`/`token:`, `Bearer `, `api_key=`/`api-key:`, and standalone `sk-` tokens.\\n- Preserve the non-secret prefix where the current contract does so and replace secret material with `[REDACTED]`.\\n- Cover repeated and multiline matches and the current short-token non-match boundary.\\n- Prove `/logs` sanitizes retained text before HTML rendering; raw secret material must not appear in the response.\\n- Do not expand or redesign redaction policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nTable-driven `sanitizeLogText` behavior tests cover each supported form, benign/empty text, repeated/multiline text, and short non-matches. A retained-log handler test asserts `[REDACTED]` is rendered and raw input is absent. Run the focused Go tests and verify the active log drawer still consumes only sanitized `LogView.Text` before approval.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:13:59.043Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:20.281Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: server.go:211-216 (sanitizeLogText) plus its two regexes at server.go:207-208 have zero test coverage — no *_test.go file references sanitizeLogText or REDACTED (verified by grep). README.md:7 and 26 state Run logs can contain sensitive repository output and must stay protected; the live-integration record on job canopy-operational-multi-repo (2026-09-02T20:10:21Z note) observed credential-linked provider output in a retained Run log. This is an observable safety behavior with no regression test where the repository convention (go test ./... gate in forest.yaml:12-15) expects coverage.\\nRequired: the redaction patterns must have deterministic unit tests proving keys/tokens/bearer strings are redacted and that benign text passes through unchanged.\\nProposed spec direction: add table-driven tests for sanitizeLogText covering each pattern branch (keys/, key_id=, token=, bearer, api_key=, sk- prefixed bearer), short-token non-matches, and multi-line logs, before or alongside the open log drawer redesign.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:13:59.043Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.474Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:04:07.474Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy renders retained Run logs after `sanitizeLogText`, but no test defends this server-side credential boundary. The open log drawer adds a copy surface over the same fragment.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- Preserve benign and empty log text unchanged.\\n- Redact every currently supported credential form: `keys/`, `key_id=`/`key-id:`, `token=`/`token:`, `Bearer `, `api_key=`/`api-key:`, and standalone `sk-` tokens.\\n- Preserve the non-secret prefix where the current contract does so and replace secret material with `[REDACTED]`.\\n- Cover repeated and multiline matches and the current short-token non-match boundary.\\n- Prove `/logs` sanitizes retained text before HTML rendering; raw secret material must not appear in the response.\\n- Do not expand or redesign redaction policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nTable-driven `sanitizeLogText` behavior tests cover each supported form, benign/empty text, repeated/multiline text, and short non-matches. A retained-log handler test asserts `[REDACTED]` is rendered and raw input is absent. Run the focused Go tests and verify the active log drawer still consumes only sanitized `LogView.Text` before approval.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:55:20.108Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:13:59.043Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering\",\n    \"title\": \"Zero-instance empty inventory page and fragment rendering lack regression cover\",\n    \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [],\n    \"lease\": {\n      \"agent\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"principal\": \"none\",\n      \"until\": \"2026-09-04T23:19:02.012Z\"\n    },\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": null,\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:37.391Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: server.go:49 (handlePage), server.go:82 (handleInstance), templates/fleet.html:36, templates/instance.html:145. Behaviors: when Canopy runs with zero configured or discovered instances, GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance must return HTTP 200 and gracefully render the empty-state templates (\\\"No instances configured.\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\", \\\"Add an instance to the inventory to begin observing it.\\\") without panic, nil pointer dereference, or HTTP 500. Failing example: initialize NewApp with Inventory{Instances: []} and issue GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance; today all tests in server_test.go initialize testInventory() with one pre-configured instance, leaving the zero-instance empty template rendering path unexercised. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in server_test.go with an empty inventory asserting that GET /, GET /fragments/fleet, and GET /fragments/instance return HTTP 200, contain the expected empty-state text (\\\"No instances configured\\\", \\\"No instance selected\\\"), and do not produce template execution errors. Observed: templates have explicit branches for empty instances (fleet.html:36, instance.html:145), but grep shows no test in server_test.go exercises an empty App inventory. Required: HTTP handler regression tests for empty-inventory page and fragment rendering. Proposed test-work: add server tests verifying that GET /, /fragments/fleet, and /fragments/instance return 200 with empty-state messages when no instances are configured.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n        \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n        \"text\": \"took\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n    \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n    \"promotions\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.276Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy supports a runtime with no configured or discovered instances, but its page and fragment routes are only tested with one configured instance. The empty operator surface can regress to a panic, 500, or broken template unnoticed.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\nWith `NewApp(Inventory{Instances: []}, ...)` and real templates:\\n\\n- `GET /` returns 200 and renders the fleet and selected-instance empty states.\\n- `GET /fragments/fleet` returns 200 and renders `No instances configured.`\\n- `GET /fragments/instance` returns 200 and renders `No instance selected` plus the instruction to add an instance.\\n- No route starts discovery, dereferences a missing selection, or requires host-specific Forest state.\\n\\nThis is test-only work; do not change empty-inventory behavior unless the scenario exposes a real defect.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nA table-driven HTTP test exercises all three routes with the actual embedded templates and an empty in-memory inventory, asserting status 200 and route-specific empty-state text. The focused server tests pass without systemd, Forest binaries, or network fixtures.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:32.84Z\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:19:02.012Z\",\n    \"derived\": {\n      \"terminal\": false,\n      \"waiting\": false,\n      \"open\": true,\n      \"live\": true,\n      \"takeable\": false\n    }\n  }\n]\n"}],"details":{}}}
