49,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":218,"totalTokens":15501,"cost":{"input":0.0098249,"output":0.00124,"cacheRead":0.00077584,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.011840739999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788549832622,"responseId":"gen-1788549832-3wnLWY3GaRlt8DRxaZWO","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_01a06de0a6c17d60b216c79a3581b073","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-tester-audit-divergence-stale\",\n  \"title\": \"Audit master commit divergence stale trust override lacks regression cover\",\n  \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy intentionally overrides a passing audit result to stale when the audited primary revision differs from the current primary revision. No observable test pins that trust signal.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- With `LastResult` pass/trusted and non-empty unequal `AuditedMaster` and `LastMaster`, the selected-instance audit badge uses the `stale` signal class.\\n- Preserve the reported pass/trusted text; stale describes revision applicability, not a rewritten audit result.\\n- Equal revisions, or a missing comparison revision, retain the result-derived class.\\n- Do not change audit classification policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nExercise `GET /fragments/instance?instance=one` with real templates and a seeded successful snapshot. Table cases cover unequal, equal, and missing revision refs. Assert 200, the rendered audit badge class, and preserved result text. Avoid source-text assertions against `auditView` internals.\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": null,\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:47.383Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy a101e023933a247460f9828b7cb8d3fce3a681ac\\nSurface: view.go:319 (auditView), templates/instance.html:40 (Audit trust metric card). Behaviors: when an instance's audited commit (AuditedMaster) differs from its current master commit (LastMaster) — indicating new commits have landed since the last audit — Canopy must classify the audit trust class as \\\"stale\\\" (signal class \\\"stale\\\") even if LastResult was \\\"pass\\\" or \\\"trusted\\\". Failing example: construct an AuditData with LastResult = \\\"pass\\\", LastMaster = \\\"sha-new\\\", and AuditedMaster = \\\"sha-old\\\", then invoke auditView or render instance.html; today no test in the repository exercises this divergence branch, leaving the critical \\\"is audited primary trustworthy?\\\" signal unpinned. Acceptance: a Builder adds a regression test proving that auditView produces TrustClass: \\\"stale\\\" when AuditedMaster and LastMaster are non-empty and unequal despite a passing LastResult, and that instance.html renders class=\\\"signal stale\\\" with the trust value. Observed: view.go:319 contains the explicit branch, but grep over all *_test.go files confirms AuditedMaster is never referenced in tests. Required: a regression test for the audit master divergence stale-override rule. Proposed test-work: add unit/template tests verifying that master revision divergence forces audit trust class to stale.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.292Z\",\n  \"promotions\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.292Z\",\n      \"by\": \"none\",\n      \"spec\": \"## Problem\\n\\nCanopy intentionally overrides a passing audit result to stale when the audited primary revision differs from the current primary revision. No observable test pins that trust signal.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- With `LastResult` pass/trusted and non-empty unequal `AuditedMaster` and `LastMaster`, the selected-instance audit badge uses the `stale` signal class.\\n- Preserve the reported pass/trusted text; stale describes revision applicability, not a rewritten audit result.\\n- Equal revisions, or a missing comparison revision, retain the result-derived class.\\n- Do not change audit classification policy in this job.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nExercise `GET /fragments/instance?instance=one` with real templates and a seeded successful snapshot. Table cases cover unequal, equal, and missing revision refs. Assert 200, the rendered audit badge class, and preserved result text. Avoid source-text assertions against `auditView` internals.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T18:58:42.895Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:06:06.292Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": true\n  }\n}\nEXIT:0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788549834862},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"Q-PaDgEe4v8ED5UZSReZ1wpui_KK6luBvcIaJhSQz_Y7-L0_wi7LKVlTqeZfQTSDyy6dDnW9cjqFF6tqEQHrFZb9v4u5itloZmJAE89MX1F8SaqqqreKArSvVGmJFj7Ny2xcVRTV4q15ePDBokBtkKp1YVT8AL2SjS4kL1BIiWp6kb7n94dphdA4B4-5iPYvw6sEDnKeCuHQlhMXnrlmzpPpIqwdPDsc3yX28-uxRFC-mDd_kzqCXikepNgs6GkxidOAIGVnL3x-sEej7jqYMOnSoC60Ebfc-j4IUnEw86-u3IRWLGhy5ijpTBp_GqhgZw7ZzYx20myfGMswxz1GWrdvjUxdXndvyZfuoWfB2KeorG9Q-6iXGePSqakMzl1iUqFByOeIjAShNursiTTpFCjX9GD7fZNgQV9if8hShoGAAkFn6W5Zf45KHabJ89-1vjm9jL_P20E7D9sqBPEhipNaDVVhaA7Y8pVp3LVH22g8tNf_8ZEsTBVJfBwlfXAxF9hxJiFKmAzqC7ofEfvs-3z9wO3reRdfTiCvB5Bz2-Zk0ngz0Tc0oYaQUQCIFRiA3Y9ybxxqFOYalISQHTvAuz0LPHjNLif-LfRyLfsMrQjviQwj9LQw1hjsJU9p3-L82aWC8SBRe2xo1RdrqvMOSnTRuaYj0XVPH-SIOIb8F_vwcNYWpeuhJxHH24c2eZ47gu9R8vBJ_5nnuIzpjRVt2yxnUnB0b4OS8rcpZ9bYZy3NM28pJ0tuevcRhdS9P-rG__KEMtH5ZEk3HcT0dwcoO4MNCTQJkXlLH3PGWjRQsCSSq_nUb7QGR4kFIZLQr03oHpEzDfvqGD6hANHRkOpzuGY4KZKK9lMuOFzUfES1mV6Hxi0h-5UVGo7kbjZYa6xG1K2lcj1y1OezA5osADK2q--oPaDZWHHzpZnj44dBcRLG2e2a0PjNaARet_t1GSeQ346NoZ-O5aafxvMiT0EMaJZjhmqShrLcbo8Lu84eMeiOH1b1F9BZIRDh6lcEk1_Y5pDLNRkMccSqUu0cd1M7XKZ0RTU4oxH